{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs5DVQudvgkWZjPqXPJw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`jsonpatch/core.py` is implemented per the spec, and the new suite under `tests/` passes: 85 tests, 0 failures (`python3 -m pytest -q tests`).\n\n- **Pointer resolution:** `resolve_pointer` follows RFC 6901, with `~1` unescaped before `~0` and strict array indices (no leading zeros, `-` rejected). Any failure raises `PointerError`.\n- **Operations:** all six (`add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy`, `test`) are implemented, with the spec's rules on `-`, `move` into its own child, and `test` equality (`1 == 1.0`, `True != 1`).\n- **Atomicity:** `apply_patch` applies every op to a deep copy and only publishes the result on success. A failed patch leaves the input unchanged, and `in_place=True` mutates the input only after success.\n\nChoices I made where the spec was silent:\n- **Removing the root** (`remove` with path `\"\"`) raises `PatchError`.\n- **`in_place` with a root type change** (for example, a dict replaced by a list) can't mutate the original object, so the new value is returned instead.\n- **`move` to the same path** is a no-op after checking that `from` exists.\n- **Patch values are deep-copied on insert,** so later ops in the same patch can't mutate the caller's patch objects.\n\nWhile re-reading the code I found that `replace` on an array index was going through the insert path, which would have shifted elements instead of overwriting them. I fixed it before the test run, and `test_replace_array_element_overwrites_not_inserts` covers it.\n\nNothing is committed; the changes are in the working tree."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8332,"cache_read_input_tokens":52237,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8332},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"65f5dc3f-4d8c-40cb-9d05-6fb5dd33f990","uuid":"1f6e9b51-fd9a-4f01-9897-cbf2ce156ec3","timestamp":"2026-10-09T17:40:29.039Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs5DV7Yj4pLhvM5Fv9Nf"}
